   5. Definitions 
   
   i. Compiler: it is a program that changes code into another form the computer can use.
   ii. Interpreter: It is a program that run code step by step instead of turning the whole program into a code first
   iii. Java Virtual Machine: it is a program thats runs Java bytecode(an instruction format only the JVM can understand and run)
   
   6. Java and Javac: javac is the compiler while java is the command that runs the compiled Java program
   
   7. ERRORS 
   i. Syntax Error: This happens when the code breaks the rule of Java, like a missing spelling of the keyword wrongly
   ii. A logic Error happens when the program runs, but it gives the wrong answer because my instructions were wrong
   
   
